Original commit body from a450ce9a8e8494ecafd8ffa29c018806e9258e02:

Analyzer half of WI-pivap (the JVM / JS sibling of Python's WI-ratid).
The base-class resolvers returned the ONLY in-repo candidate outright and
read imports only to break ties, so `import junit.framework.TestCase;
class T extends TestCase`, `import androidx.lifecycle.ViewModel; class M
: ViewModel()` and `import { Component } from 'react'` got a resolved
extends edge to an unrelated in-repo class of the same name.

- import_bound_bases (new): Java and Kotlin record each class's
  package-qualified name, so an explicitly imported base whose FQN no
  in-repo candidate has is external; the analyzer emits an unresolved
  edge with an ExternalRef, which the core linker also leaves alone.
- js_ts: no qualified names, so the specifier decides, on positive
  evidence only: a Node core module, or a registry package the
  importing package.json declares and the repo does not define.
  Workspace packages and undeclared aliases (@/models) keep the old
  resolution.

Core-linker half (qualified bases: std::exception, System.Exception,
java.util.ArrayList<T>, io.Writer) is the next PR.

